## What this site is for

{{PURPOSE}}

Every content, design and copy decision should serve that purpose. When in doubt, ask the human.

## Stack

DjangoCMS 5.x on Django 5.2 with Bootstrap 5.3 (vendored under `static/vendor/bootstrap`, no CDN),
djangocms-versioning (draft/publish), SQLite for development. Python package: `{{PROJECT_PACKAGE}}`.
Scaffolded by the `djangocms-agent` skill (`bin/new-site.py`); load that skill for CMS gotchas.

## Setup commands

    python3 -m venv venv && venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
    export DJANGO_DEBUG=1 DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=dev
    venv/bin/python manage.py migrate
    venv/bin/python manage.py seed_pages && venv/bin/python manage.py seed_site
    venv/bin/python manage.py runserver 8010

`DJANGO_DEBUG=1` is for local development only. Without it, `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` and
`DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS` must be set (see `.env.example`).

## Layout

- `{{PROJECT_PACKAGE}}/` - settings, urls, wsgi/asgi, context processor (`site_name`)
- `starter/` - app with the `HtmlBlock` plugin, seed commands (`seed_pages`, `seed_site`) and tests
- `templates/` - `base.html`, `landing.html`, `standard.html`, menu templates
- `static/` - `css/site.css`, `js/theme.js`, vendored Bootstrap
- `scripts/visual_check.py` - Playwright screenshot checker; `bin/verify.sh` - the full check

## Verification (mandatory)

Before telling a human a change works, run `bin/verify.sh` and look at the screenshots it writes to
`verify-shots/` (desktop and mobile). The final line is `VERIFY RESULT: PASS`, `FAIL` or
`INCOMPLETE`. `INCOMPLETE` means the visual step did not run (Playwright missing): report that, do
not claim the pages were visually verified. One-time setup: `pip install playwright && playwright
install chromium` (then `export PLAYWRIGHT_PYTHON=/path/to/that/python` if it is not the project venv).

Take screenshots before and after any change that affects rendering
(`python scripts/visual_check.py URL [--mobile] --out PATH`).

## CMS rules

- Seed commands are idempotent and publish through djangocms-versioning; keep them that way.
- Never invent django-cms settings: grep the installed `cms/utils/conf.py` first.
- The `starter.HtmlBlock` plugin renders raw HTML; it is for trusted editors only.

## Governance - how an AI agent should behave in this project

- Never merge, tag a release, or push to the default branch directly. Open a PR.
- Attribution and licensing matter. Say so in the PR when you bring in third-party code, and flag
  anything not compatible with this project's `{{LICENSE_SPDX}}` license.
- Propose, do not unilaterally change, governance files (this file, `CONTRIBUTING.md`,
  `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `LICENSE`).
- Security issues go through `SECURITY.md`, never a public issue or PR.
- Flag scope creep instead of just doing it.
- Never commit secrets, the database, or the admin password.
